<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/january-1">1 January</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">World's first scheduled airline flight crosses Tampa Bay</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The St Petersburg-Tampa Airboat Line flew its first paying passenger across Tampa Bay in a Benoist flying boat. The 23-minute hop launched scheduled commercial aviation, though the airline lasted only four months.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/gavrilo-princip" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gavrilo-princip.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/june-28">28 June</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Archduke Franz Ferdinand is assassinated in Sarajevo</h3><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gavrilo-princip">Gavrilo Princip</a> shot the heir to the Austro-Hungarian throne and his wife Sophie. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austro-hungarian-empire">Austria-Hungary</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austro-hungarian-ultimatum-to-serbia">ultimatum to Serbia</a> set off the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/july-crisis">July Crisis</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/austro-hungarian-empire">Austro-Hungarian Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gavrilo-princip">Gavrilo Princip</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/july-crisis">July Crisis</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/boston" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/boston.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/july-11">11 July</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Babe Ruth makes his major league debut for the Red Sox</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Nineteen-year-old Babe Ruth pitched for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boston">Boston</a> Red Sox against Cleveland, winning his first major league game. He went on to become baseball's greatest slugger and a symbol of the 1920s.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boston">Boston</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/first-world-war.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/july-28">28 July</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Austria-Hungary declares war on Serbia</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">One month after the assassination of Archduke <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/archduke-franz-ferdinand-of-austria">Franz Ferdinand</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austro-hungarian-empire">Austria-Hungary</a> declared war on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbia">Serbia</a>. Within a week <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> were drawn in, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a> had begun.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/august-1">1 August</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Germany declares war on Russia</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> refused to halt mobilisation, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> declared war on it. The declaration turned the Austro-Serbian conflict into a general European war within days.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/schlieffen-plan" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/schlieffen-plan.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/august-3">3 August</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Germany declares war on France</h3><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> declared war on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and prepared to strike through neutral <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgium">Belgium</a> under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/schlieffen-plan">Schlieffen Plan</a>. The invasion of Belgium the next day brought <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> into the war.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/german-empire">German Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/schlieffen-plan">Schlieffen Plan</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgium">Belgium</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/london" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/london.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/august-4">4 August</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Britain declares war on Germany</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">When <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> ignored an ultimatum to respect Belgian neutrality, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> declared war at 11 pm <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a> time. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-empire">British Empire</a>'s entry turned a continental war into a global one.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/british-empire">British Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/euclid" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/euclid.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/august-5">5 August</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">An electric traffic signal is installed in Cleveland</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">An electric traffic signal with red and green lights was installed at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/euclid">Euclid</a> Avenue and East 105th Street in Cleveland, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ohio">Ohio</a>. It is often cited as the first of its kind in the world.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/euclid">Euclid</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/november-1">1 November</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Von Spee's squadron defeats the Royal Navy at Coronel</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Off the coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chile">Chile</a>, Admiral Maximilian von Spee's German <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-asia">East Asia</a> Squadron sank two British cruisers, killing Rear-Admiral Cradock and some 1,600 men. It was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>'s first naval defeat in a century.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/british-empire">British Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/royal-navy">Royal Navy</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/mexican-revolution" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mexican-revolution.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/november-23">23 November</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">The last US forces withdraw from Veracruz</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The last <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> forces left the Mexican port city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/veracruz">Veracruz</a>, which they had occupied since April in response to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tampico">Tampico</a> Affair. The occupation contributed to the fall of General <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/victoriano-huerta">Victoriano Huerta</a>, who resigned in July.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexican-revolution">Mexican Revolution</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/december-24">24 December</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">The Christmas Truce begins on the Western Front</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">On <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christmas">Christmas</a> Eve, soldiers along parts of the front sang carols across the lines. Over the next day many British and German troops met in no man's land, swapped gifts and buried their dead.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/first-battle-of-the-marne" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/first-battle-of-the-marne.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Battle</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/first-battle-of-the-marne">First Battle of the Marne</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The First Battle of the Marne was fought in September 1914, when French and British forces halted the German advance towards Paris.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/simla-convention" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/simla-convention.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Treaty</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/simla-convention">Simla Convention</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Simla Convention was a treaty negotiated at Simla in 1913–1914 by representatives of Britain, China and Tibet on the status and borders of Tibet.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-cer" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-cer.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Battle</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-cer">Battle of Cer</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Battle of Cer was fought on 15–24 August 1914 on and around Mount Cer in western Serbia, when the Serbian army under Stepa Stepanović defeated the first Austro-Hungarian invasion of Serbia.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-kolubara" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-kolubara.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Battle</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-kolubara">Battle of Kolubara</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Battle of Kolubara was fought in western Serbia in November and December 1914, when the Serbian army, reorganised under Radomir Putnik and Živojin Mišić, counter-attacked an Austro-Hungarian army that had taken Belgrade.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/thomson-urrutia-treaty" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thomson-urrutia-treaty.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Treaty</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/thomson-urrutia-treaty">Thomson–Urrutia Treaty</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Thomson–Urrutia Treaty was signed in Bogotá in April 1914 by the United States and Colombia to settle the dispute caused by Panama's secession in 1903.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-bita-paka" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-bita-paka.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Battle</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-bita-paka">Battle of Bita Paka</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Battle of Bita Paka was fought on 11 September 1914 on the island of New Britain, then part of German New Guinea.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/assassination-of-archduke-franz-ferdinand" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/assassination-of-archduke-franz-ferdinand.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/assassination-of-archduke-franz-ferdinand">Assassination of Archduke Franz Ferdinand</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The assassination of Archduke Franz Ferdinand, heir to the Austro-Hungarian throne, took place in Sarajevo in 1914.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Crisis</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/austro-hungarian-ultimatum-to-serbia">Austro-Hungarian ultimatum to Serbia</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Austro-Hungarian ultimatum to Serbia was the list of demands issued by Austria-Hungary in July 1914 after the assassination of Archduke Franz Ferdinand.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Treaty</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/bryan-chamorro-treaty">Bryan–Chamorro Treaty</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Bryan–Chamorro Treaty was signed in 1914 by the US Secretary of State William Jennings Bryan and the Nicaraguan minister Emiliano Chamorro, and ratified in 1916.</p></div></li></ol></section>
