<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">In the profiles</h2><ul class="yr-prof"><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/austro-hungarian-empire"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Austro-Hungarian%20Empire.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Austro-Hungarian Empire</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Gavrilo Princip assassinates Archduke Franz Ferdinand in Sarajevo</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/german-empire"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/German%20Empire.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>German Empire</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Schlieffen Plan fails at the Marne, locking Germany into a two-front war</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/republic-of-panama"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic%20of%20Panama.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic of Panama</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Panama Canal opens on 15 August</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/kingdom-of-belgium"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Kingdom%20of%20Belgium.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Kingdom of Belgium</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Germany invades; the Belgian army holds the Yser front until 1918</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/pan-africanism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Pan-Africanism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Pan-Africanism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Marcus Garvey founds the Universal Negro Improvement Association in Jamaica</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/young-turks"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Young%20Turks.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Young Turks</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The CUP takes the Ottoman Empire into the First World War on the side of the Central Powers</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/nationalism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Nationalism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Nationalism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Serb revolutionaries in Bosnia assassinate Archduke Ferdinand, and Austria-Hungary’s attack on Serbia ignites the First World War</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/german-east-africa"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/German%20East%20Africa.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>German East Africa</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Central Railroad reaches Lake Tanganyika, and Lettow-Vorbeck's forces defeat a British force more than eight times larger at the Battle of Tanga</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/life/mustafa-kemal-ataturk"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Mustafa%20Kemal%20Atat%C3%BCrk.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Mustafa Kemal Atatürk</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Ottoman Empire enters the First World War, a step he thought a fatal mistake; at Gallipoli he commands the 19th Division and holds his position until the Allies retreat</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/first-battle-of-the-marne"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/First%20Battle%20of%20the%20Marne.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>First Battle of the Marne</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">German armies win most of the battles of the opening campaign and overrun much of Belgium and northern France</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/first-battle-of-the-marne"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/First%20Battle%20of%20the%20Marne.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>First Battle of the Marne</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The 6th Army meets the German IV Reserve Corps at the Ourcq, and the 5th Army and the BEF advance into the gap between the 1st and 2nd Armies</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/first-battle-of-the-marne"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/First%20Battle%20of%20the%20Marne.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>First Battle of the Marne</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Hentsch's staff tour leads to a general German retreat to the Aisne</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/first-battle-of-the-marne"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/First%20Battle%20of%20the%20Marne.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>First Battle of the Marne</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Moltke is replaced by Falkenhayn, and the First Battle of the Aisne begins</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/city/benin-city"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Benin%20City.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Benin City</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The British permit the restoration of the Benin monarchy</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/work/mona-lisa"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Mona%20Lisa.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Mona Lisa</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The painting, recovered after Peruggia tried to sell it in Florence, returned to the Louvre</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/work/moai"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Moai.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Moai</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Routledge expedition linked the designs on the statues' backs to the island's traditional tattooing</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/work/ishtar-gate"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Ishtar%20Gate.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Ishtar Gate</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The excavation, which had uncovered 14 metres of the gate's foundation, came to an end</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/life/marie-curie"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Marie%20Curie.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Marie Curie</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Radium Institute is built in Paris; in the war she sets up France's first military radiology centre and mobile X-ray units</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/new-culture-movement"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/New%20Culture%20Movement.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>New Culture Movement</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Zhang Shizhao founds the political magazine The Tiger in Tokyo; it runs until October 1915</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/mau-movement"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Mau%20movement.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Mau movement</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">At the outbreak of the First World War, New Zealand forces annex Western Samoa without German opposition</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/three-principles-of-the-people"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Three%20Principles%20of%20the%20People.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Three Principles of the People</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Sun reiterates the idea of a political transition in the Chinese Revolutionary Party, with an indefinite revolutionary period of party rule</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/pan-islamism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Pan-Islamism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Pan-Islamism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Pan-Islamic press has grown to well over 1000 journals, by Lothrop Stoddard’s count</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/religion/ahmadiyya"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Ahmadiyya.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Ahmadiyya</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Mirza Basheer-ud-Din Mahmood Ahmad is elected the second Caliph, and a faction opposed to him forms the Lahore Ahmadiyya Movement</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/religion/native-american-church"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Native%20American%20Church.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Native American Church</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">James Seymour of the Winnebago introduces the Half-Moon way, in 1914 or 1924</span></li></ul></section>
